Hey!

I've been playing around with ggtree -- thanks for the superb package.

I'm trying to plot a tree with additional data, like the great set up you have with the dot plot/bar chart to the side of it. But instead of having a data point for every tip label, is it possible to have a data point for node id's i.e. if I want to plot median patristic distance within a monophyletic group, I could have a dot plot next to the tree showing the median distance in each monophyletic phylogroup? I tried playing around, but couldn't figure it out!

So basically, use the node id's instead of tr$tip.label here.
tr <- rtree(30)

d1 <- data.frame(id=tr$tip.label, val=rnorm(30, sd=3))
p <- ggtree(tr)

p2 <- facet_plot(p, panel="dot", data=d1, geom=geom_point, aes(x=val), color='firebrick')
d2 <- data.frame(id=tr$tip.label, value = abs(rnorm(30, mean=100, sd=50)))

Rad package,
Edyth

